text Nagisa has started to write the play's script.
text Neither she nor I know how to write a proper script, so all she's doing is writing down her lines on a sheet of ruled paper.
text I sit next to her and quietly watch while she wrestles with each line she puts to paper.
text My hope is that doing this will make her remember something.
text But when I look at her amateurish lines, I feel as though her story gets further and further away from my initial impression of the tale, leaving me a little confused.
